# TypeScript no monorepo

## Onde colocar código novo

| Tipo | Local |
|------|-------|
| Porta (interface) | `packages/core/src/ports/` |
| Domínio, pipeline, prompt | `packages/core/src/` |
| SDK / I/O externo | `packages/adapters/src/` |
| Loader settings | `packages/config/src/` |
| SQL + repos | `packages/db/` |
| HTTP webhook | `services/webhook/` |
| Fila + pipeline | `services/worker/` |
| REST + JWT | `services/api/` |
| UI | `apps/panel/` (Épico 7) |

## Proibido no `core`

- `import` de SDK de terceiros
- `process.env` (só via settings injetados)
- I/O de rede, filesystem, Redis, Postgres

## Exemplo de wiring correto

```typescript
// services/worker — OK
import { processMessage } from '@sirvase/core';
import { createWhatsAppProvider } from '@sirvase/adapters';
import { settings } from '@sirvase/config';

// packages/core — ERRADO
import axios from 'axios'; // → criar porta + adaptador
```

## Testes

- Framework: `bun:test`
- Preferir `packages/core/test/` para domínio
- Caminho crítico obrigatório: fan-out, idempotência, isolamento de tenant
